Subject: [PATCH 08/12] marianos-azure-headless 1.10.0rc6: tests of the run
 order and the named product pages (fail on 1.10.0rc5)

From run F2's traces, before the next paid run: F2 planned the subdivisions of 25 listings above the
window and read none of them, since a subdivision was leased after every listing of the plan; with
coverage.read_product_terms on, every tile's own page would be one more request. The tests: a listing's
subdivisions are leased before the plan's next listing, and one waiting for its re-ask holds no lane; rows
read first in a chosen order with the plan unchanged; only the named products' pages read; the command
line's --rows-first and --term-upc reach the run's settings.
